{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 2, :comments ["<b>And he said.</b> Meaning, it was to them that he said thus, but his heart did not think thus." "<b>Break off.</b> Meaning, you — and not they." "<b>The golden rings.</b> And no other gold." "<b>That are in the ears.</b> If they have them on, and not lying in a chest, and not that they newly put them on, and if not this thing is a delaying factor. Also he said <b>your wives, your sons, and your daughters</b> — so as not to leave gold upon all of them, and through all this some time would elapse. Also he said <b>and bring</b> — meaning, do not send by means of a messenger; <b>to me</b> — and not to someone other than me, and not through yourselves. And his reason is that a matter done by means of many people has in it no delay, whereas by means of an individual it will be delayed somewhat; yet they were not delayed and fulfilled all the conditions except the rings. For they said, their memory for a blessing (Tanchuma), that the women did not want to, and they brought what was theirs so as not to cause delay."], :book :exodus, :voice :or-hachaim, :lang :en, :chapter 32, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T19:35:35.156288885Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}